WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.244 --> 00:00:02.410
JENNY BROWN: Find out how
the life science community

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:04.780
uses Google Cloud Platform
to organize the world's

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:07.420
genomic information while
also making it securely

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:09.250
accessible and useful.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.810
On this episode,
we'll see how it's

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.550
done through a quick
demo where you'll

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:15.730
use Google's implementation
of the htsget protocol

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:19.450
and SAMtools to create a
project using public data.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:22.270
Genomics is the study of the
genome and its environments.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.370
Today, DNA sequencing
advances have

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:27.280
made biology a data-rich
field for the first time.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.080
And the volume of
genomic data available

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.850
is growing exponentially.

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.340
Cloud genomics offers
petabyte-scale genomic data

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.020
processing and analysis.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.420
Now, let's see how this works.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.920
To get started with
this lab, you'll

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.080
have to enable the genomics API.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.860
We run some commands in Cloud
Shell to run the htsget server

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:48.340
and attach it to a local Docker
container network named "test."

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.650
We then use sequence
alignment map tools

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.920
to view statistics about a
small range on chromosome 11

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.440
on a public genome.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.370
In just a few
seconds, the SAMtools

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.440
have processed over
1,500 reads that

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:02.740
were streamed from a file
in Google Cloud Storage.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:04.629
Highly complex searches
that previously

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:06.280
could have taken
minutes are now taking

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.230
as little as four seconds.

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.060
This kind of speed
and scalability

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:12.850
is accelerating breakthroughs
in understanding the causes

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:16.360
and subtypes of conditions in
ways that can advance diagnosis

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.490
and treatment as never before.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:21.340
Qwiklabs is an online,
hands-on lab library

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:24.040
available 24 hours a
day, seven days a week,

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:27.760
with more than 150 labs on
every cloud topic, from intro

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.110
to expert level.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:32.110
Each lab helps you learn a
new skill in about 30 minutes,

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.000
using Google Cloud.

